# Security headers.
#
# The CSP ships as Report-Only ON PURPOSE. Pyodide loads its runtime with
# importScripts() from jsdelivr inside /python.worker.js and instantiates WebAssembly;
# 'wasm-unsafe-eval' should cover it on current browsers, but older Pyodide paths have
# needed 'unsafe-eval'. Enforcing this blind would break running Python, which is the
# entire product. Run Report-Only for one full nightly cycle, read the violation
# reports, then rename the header to Content-Security-Policy.
#
# Why each source is here:
#   script-src   cdn.jsdelivr.net  -> Pyodide runtime (public/python.worker.js:5)
#   worker-src   blob:             -> Pyodide spawns workers internally
#   frame-src    youtube.com       -> lesson video embeds (LessonBlock.tsx:172)
#   style-src    'unsafe-inline'   -> unavoidable: React inline style={{}} is used
#                                     app-wide. Removing it needs a nonce pipeline.
#   font-src     fonts.gstatic.com -> JetBrains Mono (index.html)
#   img-src      https:            -> OAuth avatars come from provider-chosen hosts
#                                     (Google, etc.) plus Supabase storage
#   connect-src  wss://*.supabase.co -> realtime channels (AppContext.tsx:250)
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src https://www.youtube.com https://www.youtube-nocookie.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; manifest-src 'self'

# The HTML shell must never be STORED, not merely revalidated.
#
# This said `no-cache`, which permits an intermediary to keep a copy so long as it
# revalidates. On 2026-07-30 a laptop was served an index.html referencing
# `index-yhghPmjz.js` — an entry file from neither the deployed commit nor HEAD — while
# the same URL on a phone, on a different network, loaded correctly. Same origin, same
# deployment, different path to it. Something between the two was holding an old copy and
# answering with it.
#
# `no-store` removes the ambiguity: no browser, proxy or CDN node may keep the shell at
# all. It costs one small request per navigation and it makes a stale shell impossible,
# which is worth it — a stale shell does not degrade the app, it prevents it from booting,
# and nothing inside the app is alive to recover from that.
/
  Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate
# The generated manifest, not the old hand-written manifest.json, which nothing
# links to any more.
/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/registerSW.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Hashed build assets are safe to cache forever — the name changes when they do.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
